Specifically, the following aspects of IntegratedStore were informed by reading the HACS
source:

  * The approach to registering a sidebar panel with
    `homeassistant.components.frontend.async_register_built_in_panel` using a
    `panel_custom` module entry point (see HACS `custom_components/hacs/frontend.py`).
  * The compatibility shim for static path registration across Home Assistant
    versions before and after 2024.7, where `register_static_path` was replaced by
    the asynchronous `async_register_static_paths` / `StaticPathConfig` API
    (see HACS `custom_components/hacs/utils/workarounds.py`).
  * The convention of serving downloaded Lovelace plugins from a dedicated static
    mount backed by `<config>/www/community`, rather than relying on Home
    Assistant's `/local` mapping (see HACS `custom_components/hacs/base.py`).
  * The general shape of the config flow and options flow for a store-style
    integration (see HACS `custom_components/hacs/config_flow.py`).

No HACS source code was copied verbatim into this project. All implementation in
this repository was written independently.

